WEBVTT

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:06.420
Chapter 7

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:06.420
Darcsen`s Disaster

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.790
I guess there's nothing to be said about your family line either.

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:09.820
The Defense of Fouzen will be led by Major Weber.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:14.510
I will make sure I fulfill your expectations, your Excellency.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:22.100
However, that area was originally watched over by the Militia, sir.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:27.000
Isn't it more reasonable to choose someone who has more knowledge of the area?

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.970
Don't you think that you are being arrogant?

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:36.820
Maybe you were able to raise one or two victories, but you're just a militia.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.190
Know where you stand.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:42.980
Captain Varrot.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:47.530
If you want a mission that badly, how about I send you to Barious Desert?

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:49.160
Barious Desert, sir?

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.900
But there isn't any tactical value in that...

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:55.280
There have been reports on the Imperial Army being sighted.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.160
We need some reconnaissance.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:58.370
Do you have any objections?

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:00.760
Understood, sir.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.390
It's good that you are accepting.

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:04.550
Accepting women are the best.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.000
Even I am...

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:27.790
That's just great.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.040
Wanna join in, Gregor?

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.830
There is no need for your kindness.

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:44.010
What a creep.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.470
When it comes to Gregor,

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:48.320
he's really scary.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:49.560
No way.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.950
I'm sorry, but could you go home for now?

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:53.800
But I don't want to.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.030
I'll make sure to play with you next time.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:57.180
Wait for me!

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.290
It's okay.

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:09.670
You seem to enjoy your indulgence while in His Majesty's absence.

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:12.670
It's not because he's not here. It's always like that.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:16.850
When will you get Fouzen?

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.050
It will fall in a few days.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.280
It seems a little hurried for you.

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:24.460
Trying to take back the miss at Kloden?

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:27.780
You speak as if I was incompetent.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.180
Excuse me.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:31.410
I just thought being tense isn't good.

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:33.870
A piece of advise from an old enemy.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.320
I have not forgotten.

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:40.910
The deep scar teaches me every change of season.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:43.050
Do not believe in the Black Knight.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:48.370
He is not an Imperial man, but a Fhiraldian.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:53.850
If you ask me if I am tense, it is as you think.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.870
I will destroy that tank with my own hands.

00:02:58.310 --> 00:02:59.530
Tank?

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:21.710
Just 'til then, I told him to die needlessly.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:25.820
The scariest thing in this world is a man's jealousy.

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:30.570
I can't accept the achievements of Militia's Squad 3.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:36.560
No! Why? Me, again?

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:37.810
A loss is a loss.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:38.640
Pay up, now.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.000
You're a meanie, Largo.

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:49.060
Hey, it's the young one from Squad 1.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:50.240
What's up?

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.790
Gambling is supposed to be prohibited.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.990
Well, this is...

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:58.180
C'mon. Stop that stiffness.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:01.560
Let's play together, as people who've exchanged a fight.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:03.150
I absolutey will not.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:06.880
Kept you waiting.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:10.610
It's Alicia Bakery Barious Branch's opening time.

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.340
What are you doing?

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:16.990
There was no oven, so I baked it in an iron pot instead.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:20.360
It can't compare to the real thing, but it's delicious.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:26.190
Sergeant Alicia Melchiott. You are not a baker, but a militia soldier.

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:29.100
I am a militia, but I am also a baker.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.960
If I rest, I lose my touch quickly.

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:33.780
Here you go.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:35.570
I am fine.

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:37.640
There's no need to hold back.

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:40.670
You won't grow, Sergeant Ramal Balt.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.200
It's none of your business.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:45.260
I am just searching for my squad's commander.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:46.660
Leave me alone.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:48.030
Faldio?

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:50.610
Then, I'll look for him with you.

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:51.440
Eh?!

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:53.260
It's okay.

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:55.230
No refusing.

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:56.990
Uh.. W-Wait...

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:56.990
Well, let's get going.

00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:58.680
Come on. Get walking.

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:05.720
Isara, is Welkin here?

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:08.050
No, he hasn't come here.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:09.700
What might it be?

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:15.440
The person I am searching for is Commander Faldio Landzaat.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:18.660
It's not the Squad 7's commander.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:22.420
Faldio is not here, and neither is Welkin, then...

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:23.600
I got it.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:28.540
Isara, what has Welkin been sketching recently?

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:29.590
Sketch?

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:32.910
Oh, if you mean that...

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:37.060
What do you think?

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:41.930
Isn't it more likely an unexpected accident than a planned action?

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:46.390
From an archaeological viewpoint, that is a little hard to agree with.

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:52.480
From old scriptures, the Darcsen Calamity was definitely caused by people with their minds on it.

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:54.650
Welkin!

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:56.460
Faldio!

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.600
Did you find the bat lizard yet?

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:00.830
Nope. Not yet, unfortunately.

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:04.110
How did you know about the bat lizard?

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:08.930
Both of you were on leave.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:12.910
I thought that meant Faldio was keeping you company for your sketching.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:16.610
Ingenious. That's amazing detective work there.

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:20.560
It means that she cares a lot about us every day.

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:21.560
Right?

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.340
Sorry to disappoint you.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:25.600
The one who cares is him.

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:27.670
What's up, Ramal?

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:35.800
It's a little hard to say it here, sir.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:37.460
Don't worry.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:39.500
They are all reliable comrades.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.560
They won't go busting out your confession everywhere.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:44.340
They aren't comrades!

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:50.010
Squad 7 lacks self-awareness as soldiers.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:54.090
Aren't you a little high just because you've become a little famous?

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:56.100
Wait, why would you put it that...

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.810
Above all, a Squad with a Darcsen...

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:01.040
Look here.

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:02.290
Good timing.

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:02.900
Huh?

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:07.610
Would you guys give us your opinions about the Darcsen Calamity?

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:15.160
A short while ago, we were in a sophisticated and profound discussion about the truth of the event.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:18.190
W-Wait a sec.

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:20.420
Is that something to talk about in a place like this?

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:23.390
Don't you guys think that it's strange?

00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:27.370
It was an event that happened around this area only 2000 years ago.

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:29.190
That's right, Ramal!

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:34.450
Right now, we are next to historic ground: the Barious Ruins!

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:39.100
To me, it is nothing more than a location we were sent to for patrol mission.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:42.230
Come on, you are such an apathetic kid.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:46.150
Well, isn't it more of a myth than a legend?

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:49.400
Hey, hey. Are you telling me that it's made up?

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.250
That's incorrect.

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:55.360
Over there are remains of towns burnt down by the Darcsen.

00:07:55.960 --> 00:08:02.020
Darcs burnt the land, and the Valkyria felled the Darcs.

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.790
This is a historical truth.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:06.830
Ah, about that, Faldio.

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:12.350
I think the part about Darcsen destroying the town on their own will was something that was added later.

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:13.590
Right, Isara?

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:21.560
Yes. If I was living in the past, I don't think I would do something to destroy my own properties.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:25.640
Hm. You are saying that it makes no logical sense.

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:30.420
The fact that Darcsens themselves left no records of the event is awkward as well.

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:35.710
To be frank, that is one fact that many historians point out.

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:38.010
Isara is quite a debater.

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:40.840
Well, I have confidence in arguing my points as well.

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:42.720
Let me ask you, Isara...

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:44.380
Wait a moment.

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:46.360
You three are ignoring Ramal and me.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:48.650
So, let's all think together.

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:51.080
After you heard our thoughts, what do you think?

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:53.080
Huh?

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:07.970
The Ragnite Refinery is currently at 50% of normal production output due to labor shortage.

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:13.040
There are a lot of Darcsens.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:15.560
Yes, sir. About three out of ten villagers are.

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:31.880
So, the Darcsen students and children younger than fourteen were exempt from the conscription, right?

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.810
We should make them work as well.

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:36.720
But that is...

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:42.330
Ragnite is the backbone of our nation. We must maintain our production quota.

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:47.340
Oh right. Did you get the Militia to withdraw?

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:49.410
Yesterday, sir.

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:50.550
That's well done.

00:09:50.550 --> 00:09:54.920
The Militia is just a burden to the Regulars.

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:01.490
Today, I will make sure to get Welkin's idea straight.

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:02.830
Excuse me, sir.

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:06.870
Commander, did you bring all of them?

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:10.800
Yeah. We were luckily sent to the Barious region.

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:14.370
If I can do some at-site investigation, I should be able to find something.

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:17.900
What is it? What's wrong?

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:21.950
Is it their fault that you have changed, sir?

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:23.320
Their?

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:25.110
It's Squad 7.

00:10:25.110 --> 00:10:27.310
Those irresponsible good-for-nothings.

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:31.800
So that's it. I've changed?

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:35.240
If you say so, maybe I have.

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:37.220
Do not take the Fouzen thing too deep.

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:38.080
But...

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:43.660
I understand your feelings about why we are letting go of a fight that we can win at.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.910
But that's how the higher-ups work.

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:50.990
As long as they don't get the bitterness, they won't understand it.

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:53.600
Bitterness...

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:56.150
What do you think? Do you think we can win?

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:58.380
T-That is...

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:00.300
I have the same opinion.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:01.990
Weber will lose.

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:05.010
Let's go, Ramal.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:07.280
It's a holiday for the warriors.

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:11.290
Well then...

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:15.210
We will be back by 1900.

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:17.350
Yeah, yeah. I got ya.

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:21.050
Even so, to a place like that, you've got some taste.

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:22.480
Really.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:27.710
If we find any new facts, I will address my thanks to you.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:37.080
Why am I here?

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:39.090
Isn't it good with flowers on your sides?

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:40.080
This is not the time to joke...

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:41.640
Um, sir.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:43.360
I hear a strange noise.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:45.210
What did you say?

00:11:57.390 --> 00:11:59.810
Damn it. That's no good.

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:02.520
I think it's the carburetor, sir.

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:03.950
You know it well.

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:05.670
This is my specialty.

00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:09.530
It should have been around ten to fifteen minutes by car from here.

00:12:09.530 --> 00:12:12.300
Giving up after we've come so far seems like a let-down.

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:14.220
Couldn't we walk there?

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:16.670
You guys should go ahead.

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:19.300
I'll wait here with Hans.

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:23.430
Maybe I'll be able to fix it.

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:26.520
You can do that later, so let's go together.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:31.400
Isara, are you thinking about the legend?

00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:39.430
It's not that I care much about it, but if there is someone who would feel bad, it's best to hold myself back.

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:42.420
What do you mean by that? Are you trying to rub it in me?

00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:45.230
Are you sure you don't want to go?

00:12:45.230 --> 00:12:47.330
Yes. I'll wait here.

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:52.500
Isara's a stubborn girl.

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:55.050
We'll leave it to you here, then.

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:07.930
I will stay behind, sir.

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:10.090
Huh? Why?

00:13:10.090 --> 00:13:14.330
There is a need to keep an eye on whether or not the enemy's here.

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:19.620
I wonder what happened.

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:23.890
Fear, curiosity and likings are similar in nature.

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:24.820
What?

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:28.260
In other words, Ramal is worried about Isara.

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:28.680
Eh?

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:29.380
Eh?

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:33.840
Hey, hey. Welkin aside, you shouldn't be surprised, Alicia.

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:37.380
Huh? But that kid loves you so much.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:40.690
That is that, and this is this, you can say.

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:47.930
In other words, Alicia's "in love with Faldio" is like how in a wolf's pack, they all obey the leader...

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:49.680
Welkin, just shut up.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:50.450
Eh?

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:52.230
I can see it.

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:27.550
It's not like I came because of you.

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:28.600
Huh?

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:30.320
Fix it quickly.

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:31.410
It's easy, right?

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:32.940
Ah. Yes.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:44.890
Wow.

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:52.060
The reason why it's bright even with no light coming in is because there are ragnite crystals mixed into the walls?

00:14:52.060 --> 00:14:56.010
Yes. It means that it was created after they were mined.

00:14:56.620 --> 00:15:00.860
Hey, there are symbol-like things engraved.

00:15:00.860 --> 00:15:03.410
Those are archaic letters.

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:08.440
This place served not only as a sacred ground but also as a library to the Valkyrians.

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:09.720
Library?

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:15.110
Scripture on one wall is a record on the calamity between the Darcsens and the Valkyrians.

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:20.370
Yes, it is a detestable story.

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:25.690
What may "detestable" be directed to?

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:33.940
To all. To Valkyrians, Darcsens, and all of the world, it is a detestable and foolish story.

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:41.240
The greedy one took all of the fruits, seeds and livestock for themselves.

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:48.410
That is it. On top of that, it is said that they have scorched the Barious Plain with an evil power.

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:51.790
Continue on, Selvaria.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:58.560
The courageous one was deeply saddened and angered and pointed the spear to the greedy one.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:04.070
With the spear clad in blue flames, she impaled his heart.

00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:07.350
And the lands became fertile once more.

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:13.500
This place is a remain of the Darcsen village that they burned themselves.

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:19.170
It is told that Valkyrians built this temple with an intention to soothe the souls of those who were lost.

00:16:19.170 --> 00:16:22.710
But why did the Valkyrians die out?

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:25.550
They had great powers, right?

00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:30.430
The Darcsen Calamity was only a mere two millenia ago.

00:16:30.430 --> 00:16:34.120
The time seems too short for a natural extinction.

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:37.660
Gallia's Archduke, the Randgriz Family,

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:40.720
has been told to have inherited the bloods of Valkyrians,

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:47.190
but at the moment, who the Valkyrians were is the greatest enigma of all.

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:51.210
If all of these walls are decrypted, will the enigma be solved as well?

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:52.910
No.

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:57.010
The Darcsen Calamity itself has a lot of missing records.

00:16:57.010 --> 00:16:58.570
I guess that's so.

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:12.340
Valkyria.

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:40.080
What?

00:17:46.890 --> 00:17:48.420
Are you okay, Alicia?

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:51.360
I'm astounded. There was more inside?

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:57.220
What is this?

00:17:58.530 --> 00:18:00.310
What the heck is this?

00:18:01.170 --> 00:18:02.770
Alicia!

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:04.520
Are you a goddess of good fortune?

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:06.270
For such a thing to happen...

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:07.290
Faldio?

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:08.820
Wait, what's going on?

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:11.790
Totally new engravements appeared.

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:15.580
With this, we may be able to figure out who the Valkyrians are.

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:18.480
History will make a great leap forward.

00:18:18.480 --> 00:18:20.240
C-Congratulations.

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:21.800
Wait, Faldio.

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:27.280
It will one day be exposed to eyes of many.

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:30.330
Even if I enjoyed it alone right now, I won't do anyone wrong.

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:32.480
But we don't know what might be there.

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:33.750
It's dangerous.

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:35.380
Are you telling me to stay?

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:36.720
That would be good for you.

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:41.750
And that's why you let an old geezer like Damon take name for your work.

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:43.440
Faldio...

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:46.050
If you don't feel like it, you head back first.

00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:47.480
I am going.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:48.830
I'll go as well.

00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:49.940
Alicia?

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:52.240
Come on! We are the first!

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:54.020
Isn't this really great?

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:55.650
Well, but...

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:56.570
Come on.

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:05.750
So... The legendary sacred ground is actually that place.

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:07.310
Your Majesty.

00:19:07.310 --> 00:19:08.650
What is it?

00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:09.770
There is someone.

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:34.470
What's up, Faldio?

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:37.050
Oh, it's nothing.

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:38.270
Really?

00:19:38.270 --> 00:19:41.040
Hey, tell me what's written there.

00:19:41.040 --> 00:19:42.060
Somebody's here.

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:49.450
Perhaps Isara and Ramal have come after us.

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:56.780
Who is it?

00:19:57.330 --> 00:20:01.340
If you want our name, it is polite to give yours first.

00:20:10.630 --> 00:20:17.740
S-Sorry. I am Karl Landzaat, but even if I told you I don't think anyone would know me.

00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:20.990
I'm the rather plain looking one with glasses and a butch.

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:26.730
I have been thinking that I can work in Squad 7, because the commander is laid back.

00:20:26.730 --> 00:20:31.770
Next on Valkyria Chronicles: Chapter 8 - Scrutinized History.

00:20:31.770 --> 00:20:37.120
C-Catchphrase? T-Then, "Diligence is best!"

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:40.000
Chapter 8

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:40.000
Scrutinized History

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:39.320
S-Sorry for being lame.
